# terminus: Terminus, a bitmap font drawn for reading on a console, at all
# nine of its heights from 12 to 32 pixels, regular and bold. This is the
# font set vtium draws when no font is named. Drawing it needs no outline
# rendering, so it suits a small or slow machine.
#
# Each source= line and its strike= lines are one font at several heights,
# and vtium draws each character cell from the tallest strike that fits it.
# When nothing sets the cell's size, vtium takes the cell of the tallest
# strike no taller than the size it would choose for the display, so each
# glyph fills its cell. Above 32 pixels the cell is a whole multiple of the
# 32-pixel strike's cell, and the 32-pixel strike draws at that multiple. A
# cell under 12 pixels, such as the 8-pixel rows of a 320×240 panel, draws
# vtium's built-in font, because no strike is that short.
#
# GNU Unifont, the unifont layer, draws every character that Terminus lacks,
# such as Han, kana and Hangul, in cells of 16 pixels and more. The set
# names no symbols or emoji layer, because both are outline fonts: Unifont
# draws emoji in 1 bit, and a Nerd Fonts icon draws as a hollow box. The
# font set cullet-mono adds color emoji and the icons.
#
# Every vtium build installs these files: upstream's BDF files, each
# gzipped with gzip -n -9, so each sha256= line is the hash of the gzipped
# file.
#
# License: Terminus is under the SIL OFL 1.1, with the Reserved Font Name
# "Terminus Font": Copyright (C) 2020 Dimitar Toshkov Zhekov. The layer
# names its own license.
#
# References:
# - ADR-1204 D2: the bitmap set, its strikes and the cell they give.
# - ADR-1204 D7: the version=, sha256= and url= lines.

name=terminus
license=OFL-1.1

